I wrote this very small patch after receiving the following YAFMC ;)

  Version mismatch for file "bonM0.8".
  Discarding unuseable bones; no need to panic...

If you are compiling under DOS, be advised that running setup.bat renames
patchlevel.h to patchlev.h, so you should apply this patch immediately
after unpacking the source code.

Michael


=========cut here=============
diff -u -r nethack-3.4.2/include/patchlevel.h
340bones/include/patchlevel.h
--- nethack-3.4.2/include/patchlevel.h	Fri Aug 29 20:07:22 2003
+++ 340bones/include/patchlevel.h	Sun Sep 14 11:16:00 2003
@@ -34,7 +34,7 @@
  * PP = patch level, ee = edit level, L = literal suffix "L",
  * with all four numbers specified as two hexadecimal digits.
  */
-#define VERSION_COMPATIBILITY 0x03040100L
+#define VERSION_COMPATIBILITY 0x03040000L
 #endif


